From be06ecfc287989914338b34fb80bcb6521346c69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:39:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): log sidebar status-stripe transitions with
 their row inputs [daveey]

Rows keep getting reported green (done) while kanban work is still queued, and
by the time anyone looks they are right again. Each sidebar row now writes one
desktop.log line 'stripe-transition <sid> old->new' when its stripe changes,
with conn/profile, dot state, kanban_active/parked/held/blocked/waiting_on,
kanban_observed_at, goal_active, background_active, async delegation and
background-running claims, and the row's source (sessions.changed /
list-refetch / window-sessions-changed / project-tree / cache). First sighting
only records; capped at 6 lines per session per minute with a suppressed count.
---
